  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Alice is visiting the amusement park!\n\nAlice's height is XXX centimeters.\n\nThe park stipulates that the minimum height necessary to get on the giant wheel is 606060 centimeters.\n\nWill Alice be able to ride on the giant wheel?\n\n\nInput Format\nThe only line of input contains a single integer XXX — Alice's height.\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nOutput the answer on a single line: `\"Yes\"` if Alice can ride the giant wheel, and `\"No\"` otherwise (without quotes).\n\n\nEach letter of the output may be printed in either uppercase or lowercase, i.e, the strings `NO`, `no`, `No`, and `nO` will all be treated as equivalent.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤X≤1001 \\leq X \\leq 1001≤X≤100"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "59",
        "output": "No",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nAlice's height is 595959 centimeters, which is less than the minimum height of 606060.\nSo, she can't ride the giant wheel."
      },
      {
        "id": "sample_2",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "60",
        "output": "Yes",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nAlice's height is 606060 centimeters, which equals the minimum height of 606060.\nSo, she can ride the giant wheel."
      },
      {
        "id": "sample_3",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "61",
        "output": "Yes",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nAlice's height is 606060 centimeters, which is greater than the minimum height of 606060.\nSo, she can ride the giant wheel."
      }
    ]
  },
